    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do F connectors differ from other coaxial connectors?",
        "answer": "F connectors use the coaxial cable's own centre conductor as the mating pin, avoiding a separate machined centre contact. This makes them simple and cost-effective for satellite TV. BNC, N-type, and custom connectors use dedicated contacts and are selected for different impedance, environmental, or application requirements."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are 90-degree and right-angle connectors different?",
        "answer": "No. Both names describe an F connector that turns the cable path by 90 degrees for tight receiver installations. \"Right angle\" is common in Europe and \"90 degree\" in North America; the part follows the same IEC 61169-24 dimensions and 75-ohm impedance target."
      },
      {
        "question": "How should outdoor satellite cable connectors be fitted?",
        "answer": "Use a compression F connector for durable weatherproofing. Strip the cable without damaging the 15mm braid or 10mm centre conductor, fold the braid over the jacket, seat the dielectric flush, and compress fully with the correct tool. Keep braid clear of the centre conductor and seal the dish-end connection with self-amalgamating tape."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which plating is best for outdoor dish connectors?",
        "answer": "Nickel on C3604 brass is the standard outdoor choice: 3&ndash;5&micro;m for sheltered positions and 5&ndash;8&micro;m for fully exposed coastal, humid, or industrial sites. Seal exposed dish-end connectors with self-amalgamating tape. Flash gold, 0.1&ndash;0.5&micro;m over nickel, is better suited to premium indoor mating surfaces."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are typical order quantities?",
        "answer": "Consumer connector development normally begins at 500&ndash;1,000 pieces and scales to tens of millions annually. Aerospace and satellite-radio prototypes typically begin at 100&ndash;500 pieces, with flexibility for custom development. Blanket orders can provide stable monthly deliveries and pricing."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can twin and right-angle connectors run together?",
        "answer": "Yes. Straight F, twin, 90-degree, right-angle, and aerial connectors can run as a mixed programme on the same Swiss CNC platform. This lets distributors consolidate sourcing, logistics, and quality documentation across their connector range."
      }
    ]
